{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack","id":842676,"title":"What if Father Wolf wasn't weakened by the first Pack...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-05T12:21:21-08:00","id":842676,"title":"What if Father Wolf wasn't weakened by the first Pack...","content":"...But instead by breaking the Silver Ladder. The Abyss is a barrier between the Supernal and Phenomenal worlds. The Gauntlet is between the World and the Shadow. The Silver Ladder could have been resting partially in the Border Marches as a sort of sympathetic model of the bridging between both the Supernal and Phenomenal. And Father Wolf as a guardian of borders could have recognized the disruption caused by material beings entering the Supernal and rallied some mages and with their help assaulted the bridge between worlds. In the process he collapsed the Marches into the Gauntlet and tore the Abyss open cutting off the movement between the worlds. But because their was no longer a proper hunting ground between the Shadow and the Flesh he could not adequately perform his duties. So he let himself die so his legacy, the Uratha, could live on.<br /> <br /> I think the only evidence for this is the stories of the Aegis Kai Doru who blame Mages and Werewolves for something. If the Aegis was originally another prefall civilization they could have blamed the Atlanteans and the First pack for the war which damaged their own magics? Any thoughts on this explanation for the World of Darkness? I like it because it makes several of the cosmologies relevant to understanding the world. Just that Werewolves don't know why they had to kill Father Wolf and Mages don't like to admit that they were massive idiots who screwed everything up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:37:31-08:00","id":842683,"title":"","content":"Well, since the Neolithic chapter in Dark Eras is post Fall but pre Sundering, it's safe to say that they were not the same event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:10:10-08:00","id":842695,"title":"","content":"Consider that the Sundering (presumably) affected the world through all Arcana - it's possible that Father Wolf weakening (and eventual death) occurred long before the event that caused his weakness.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the earliest of what would become the Pure spent their first years/decades/centuries trying to work out how to prevent the magical cataclysm that was still to come, and those who would be Forsaken pushed for the event. For true time-bendy stuff, perhaps the actions of the Pure failed in a way that caused what they were trying to prevent.<br /> <br /> It may not be canon, but I could see some interestingly brain-twisting games come out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:11:53-08:00","id":842696,"title":"","content":"First off, Celestial Ladder.<br /> <br /> Secondly, The Fall is always before every other event, and at the same time it never actually happened. You can go back through the whole of history and never find Atlantis, though you may find ruins that suggest 20 different kinds of Atlantis. As Charly says, our earliest setting, in 5500~BCE with the Vinca civilization, pre-Sundering, still has mages looking back and finding nothing, but shards of impossible space-times that suggest otherwise.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, regardless of if it's true or not, I like the idea that the AKD's problems stem from King Lycaon. Modernly, it's the just the principle of both parties dividing mankind from their paradise more and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-05-2016, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:53:02-08:00","id":842708,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the answer to this question is basically: in &quot;canon&quot;, loose though it is, the Fall happened before the Sundering, but you can say it didn't for your game, just like you can houserule pretty much anything else as being true or not, mechanically or setting-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:59:26-08:00","id":842713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842708#post842708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the answer to this question is basically: in &quot;canon&quot;, loose though it is, the Fall happened before the Sundering, but you can say it didn't for your game, just like you can houserule pretty much anything else as being true or not, mechanically or setting-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, Max, and while there's a good amount of rejiggering to do it, it's one of the more hackable setting conceits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:01:28-08:00","id":842716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842683#post842683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since the Neolithic chapter in Dark Eras is post Fall but pre Sundering, it's safe to say that they were not the same event.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's possible that the Fall weakened Father Wolf, he then wouldn't be killed until the Sundering.<br /> <br /> I'm still a proponent of the belief that humanity's turn towards agriculture and placing less emphasis on hunting is what weakened him, in addition to the other more traditional reasons. Fighting things like the Spinner Hag and the Plague King especially when, with the rise of humanity, those things may have become increasingly powerful as they were effectively worshiped by mankind. Other things, too. In the Ivory Claws legends, Silver Wolf was the first to see the weakness in his father and attempted to usurp him, and was put down mightily for it. While Silver Wolf failed, Father Wolf's bane was still the fang and claw of his children, which Silver Wolf was one of.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of little legends and reasons why it might have happened, but I don't think it has anything to do with the Fall. It's possible the Neolithic age expansion will expand on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-05-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:05:31-08:00","id":842717,"title":"","content":"Humanity going to an agricultural model of society has been supported by Chris as a really big factor for Wolf going down, I <i>think</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:18:30-08:00","id":842722,"title":"","content":"Or weird time stuff where in the no longer existent timeline when Atlantis did exist he weakened because he destroyed the Celestial Ladder but in the actual history he just sort of weakened gradually for no clear reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:20:19-08:00","id":842724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842716#post842716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it's possible that the Fall weakened Father Wolf, he then wouldn't be killed until the Sundering.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though since the Fall happened in a time that no longer ever existed, Father Wolf would have to have been weakened since the beginning of time (or, the beginning of this version of it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842716#post842716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still a proponent of the belief that humanity's turn towards agriculture and placing less emphasis on hunting is what weakened him, in addition to the other more traditional reasons. Fighting things like the Spinner Hag and the Plague King especially when, with the rise of humanity, those things may have become increasingly powerful as they were effectively worshiped by mankind. Other things, too. In the Ivory Claws legends, Silver Wolf was the first to see the weakness in his father and attempted to usurp him, and was put down mightily for it. While Silver Wolf failed, Father Wolf's bane was still the fang and claw of his children, which Silver Wolf was one of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that interpretation, and I'm pretty sure it's been supported by a couple of writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842716#post842716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of little legends and reasons why it might have happened, but I don't think it has anything to do with the Fall. It's possible the Neolithic age expansion will expand on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's currently still open to interpretation, but hopefully we'll know more once Dark Eras is out.<br /> <br /> And, of course, obligatory &quot;if you want the Fall to have been the cause, it can be in your games.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:21:37-08:00","id":842725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842722#post842722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or weird time stuff where in the no longer existent timeline when Atlantis did exist he weakened because he destroyed the Celestial Ladder but in the actual history he just sort of weakened gradually for no clear reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely possible from what we know so far. Not my favorite interpretation, but definitely one with implications worth exploring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:29:06-08:00","id":842729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842724#post842724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, though since the Fall happened in a time that no longer ever existed, Father Wolf would have to have been weakened since the beginning of time (or, the beginning of this version of it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> Any ways considering enter the Supernal basically just erases you from existence and Supernal entities don't seem to have any interest in entering the real world it doesn't seem like acting as a border guard for them would be a big deal.<br /> <br /> I view the Fall as a Tower of Babel-like reaction from the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-05-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:44:46-08:00","id":842737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842717#post842717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity going to an agricultural model of society has been supported by Chris as a really big factor for Wolf going down, I <i>think</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain that's explicitly called out in a few things he said in the spoilers thread on the Mage forums. Maybe the one discussing the Neolithic Dark Era in this forum- not sure exactly, there was a fair bit of cross-posting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:37:33-08:00","id":842770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=842713#post842713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, Max, and while there's a good amount of rejiggering to do it, it's one of the more hackable setting conceits.</div> </div> </div> </div>...who is Max? But yeah, 2e probably makes it more viable because it establishes The Fall and Atlantis (if it existed) as being &quot;out of time&quot; in a way that even though they're described as happening &quot;before anything else&quot;, they could have influenced events non-linearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:39:26-08:00","id":842773,"title":"","content":"Max is heroine of Life is Strange. At one point, one her classmates says to her &quot;This is true, Max.&quot; It stuck with me for reasons I cannot fathom, and now when I say &quot;This is true&quot;, it must invariably be followed up with &quot;Max.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: It occurs to me it might have deeper roots going back to my childhood love of Sam and Max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T03:36:49-08:00","id":843351,"title":"","content":"It's possible Father Wolf didn't even <i>exist</i> &quot;before&quot; the Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T08:18:33-08:00","id":843447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/842676-what-if-father-wolf-wasn-t-weakened-by-the-first-pack?p=843351#post843351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible Father Wolf didn't even <i>exist</i> &quot;before&quot; the Fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unpack that a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:19:22-08:00","id":843475,"title":"","content":"Well, we don't know much other than the Exarchs-to-be basically broke reality. That erased an entire civilisation from existence and created the Abyss.Who knows what else changed? Reality as we know it might be unrecognisable compared to what came before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T23:41:28-07:00","id":859494,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the first pack (Now officially NOT the First Born...dangit) simply became too ravenous and decided to kill dad because they could... They are his bane after all, isn't it their right to slay him in his weakness? As for why he was weakening... maybe he WAS from the Time before (there is SOME evidence to support that) or maybe his essence was tied to his descendants' numbers OR maybe his health was tied to the withering Pangea OR to the fact that humanity had moved beyond Hunting (though that kind of insinuates that Wolf was far more of a spirit than a GOD). <br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, it shows that the pure (specifically the Kings) have a point in their jihad (though not really, because they're psycho looney)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0